			<div class="content" id="post-content-1404757">
									

<p>I think this is a truly interesting idea, especially since the real horror (for me, at least) lies in the idea that Eugenio is one of at least two, but possibly more (MANY more) hyper-intelligent animals.<br />
One question, though: why exactly is it classified as Keter? It seems to be making no concentrated effort to escape, and without the ability to marshal other animals it kind of seems to lack real destructive power. And even if it escapes, it's not like humans don't have both the desire and means to hunt down Eugenio's noblemen and serfs.</p>

